### FantasyIQ manual API testing collection
### Run `docker compose up -d` + `./gradlew bootRun` first.
### In IntelliJ, run requests top to bottom with the "Run All Requests" gutter action,
### or click the individual green arrows -- {{accessToken}}/{{refreshToken}} are
### captured automatically from prior responses via the client.global scripts below.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### Register
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "coach@fantasyiq.dev",
  "password": "correct-horse-battery",
  "displayName": "Coach"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### Register again with the same email -- expect 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "coach@fantasyiq.dev",
  "password": "correct-horse-battery",
  "displayName": "Coach"
}

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "coach@fantasyiq.dev",
  "password": "correct-horse-battery"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### Login with wrong password -- expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "coach@fantasyiq.dev",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Refresh -- rotates the token pair
# @name refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("oldRefreshToken", client.global.get("refreshToken"));
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### Replay the old (now rotated-out) refresh token -- expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{oldRefreshToken}}"
}

### Trigger player ingestion from ESPN (requires auth; pulls all 32 rosters, can take a while)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/players/ingest
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Search players by (partial) name
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/players/search?q=mahomes
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get a player by id -- replace with a real id from the search response above
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/players/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get a player's trending/usage-delta signal -- same UsageTrendFactorCalculator the
### scoring engine uses, run against their 4 most recent games with no season/week
### boundary. Player-game-stats must already be ingested; a player with fewer than 4
### games gets a response with a null contribution/narrative, not a 404.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/players/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/trending
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Trigger schedule ingestion from ESPN for the CURRENT season (requires auth;
### regular-season games only -- may return 0 if ESPN hasn't published the slate yet)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/games/ingest
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Trigger schedule ingestion for a SPECIFIC season (e.g. last season's completed
### games, so player-game-stats ingestion below has something real to link against)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/games/ingest?season=2025
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Trigger injury ingestion from ESPN (requires auth; run /api/players/ingest FIRST --
### reports for players not yet ingested are silently skipped, not an error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/injuries/ingest
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Trigger player game-stats ingestion for a completed season (requires auth;
### run /api/players/ingest AND /api/games/ingest?season=<year> FIRST -- per-athlete,
### QB/RB/WR/TE only, hundreds of HTTP calls so this can take several minutes)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/player-game-stats/ingest?season=2025
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Compute defense-vs-position stats for a specific week (requires auth; no external
### call -- pure aggregation, run /api/player-game-stats/ingest for the same season FIRST)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/defense-vs-position/compute?season=2025&week=1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Trigger weather forecast ingestion for a specific week (requires auth; run
### /api/games/ingest?season=<year> FIRST -- skips dome/fixed-roof stadiums, kickoffs
### outside OpenWeatherMap's ~5-day forecast window, and kickoffs already in the past.
### Needs OPENWEATHER_API_KEY set -- without a real key every call eventually returns
### 503 once the circuit breaker trips)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/weather/ingest?season=2025&week=1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Trigger betting-line ingestion (requires auth; no season/week params -- The Odds API
### only exposes the current slate of upcoming games, matched against ours by team names
### + closest kickoff. Run /api/games/ingest for the current season FIRST so there's
### something to match against. Needs ODDS_API_KEY set -- without a real key eventually
### returns 503 once the circuit breaker trips)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/odds/ingest
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Generate start/sit recommendations for a specific week (requires auth; no external
### call -- pure composition over already-ingested/computed data. Run games/injuries/
### player-game-stats/defense-vs-position/weather/odds ingestion for the same season
### FIRST for the richest factor coverage, though any subset works -- each factor is
### independently optional, and a player with zero available factors gets no row at all)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recommendations/generate?season=2025&week=1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Read already-computed start/sit recommendations for a week, sorted by score
### descending (requires auth; position filter optional)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recommendations/start-sit?season=2025&week=1&position=WR
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Backtest: (re)generates start/sit recommendations for every week of a completed
### season, then correlates predicted scores against real fantasy points from
### player_game_stats (requires auth; run player-game-stats/ingest for the full
### season FIRST). Takes a while -- it's re-running /generate for every week with
### games. Injury-overridden recommendations are excluded from the correlation --
### see BacktestResult's own doc comment for why.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recommendations/backtest?season=2025
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Weight tuning: pure read-only analysis over whatever recommendations already exist
### for the season (run /generate or /backtest FIRST -- this does not regenerate
### anything itself). For each continuous factor (MATCHUP/VEGAS/WEATHER/USAGE), fits a
### regression of actual points against that factor's current contribution --
### suggestedScaleMultiplier close to 1.0 means already well-calibrated, higher means
### under-weighted. Factors with no matched data (e.g. VEGAS/WEATHER for a historical
### season with no betting_lines/weather_forecasts) report null, not zero.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recommendations/tune-weights?season=2025
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
